From 1ff10844f72b8b89a22cc76b0a2b0803fbb5e134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LineageOS builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:19:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Updater: Unattended installation of updates

Off unless the system property lineage.updater.auto_install is true, and
only on non-A/B devices (recovery install path); with the property unset
nothing new is scheduled and the app behaves as before.

When enabled:
- BOOT_COMPLETED schedules a one-shot check; a check that found no
  validated network is retried instead of dropped.
- The candidate is only ever the newest update from the server that is
  newer than the running build and of the same SDK level; if it was
  tried automatically before, there is no candidate (no fallback to an
  older build).
- After a successful check the candidate is downloaded by UpdaterService
  on an unmetered network, after a free-space check. Download errors
  are resumed after 30 min, 1, 2, 4 and 8 h, then not before the next
  check.
- A verified package is installed by two jobs: device idle + charging,
  and device idle inside the night window 00:00-05:00. Right before
  installing, the package's own signed metadata must show a newer
  build, the same SDK level and a non-A/B package (the index JSON is
  unsigned); the screen must be off, the battery level OK and the space
  for the uncrypt copy free.
- The ids of attempted packages are stored (commit()) before the install
  is triggered, when verification fails and when the metadata refuses
  the package; they are never tried automatically again, which prevents
  reboot and download loops. The user can still install them by hand.
- A 15 min partial wake lock covers the copy for uncrypt until the
  reboot.

Workers start UpdaterService as a foreground service (allowed from the
background by START_ACTIVITIES_FROM_BACKGROUND); the service goes
foreground at once for these intents and drops it again when nothing
was started. The rules are pure functions in AutoInstallPolicy; every
decision is logged once under the tag AutoInstall. No new strings or
permissions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
